# Cursor Rules — NextJS + ExpressJS Turborepo Monorepo

This is a full-stack Turborepo monorepo with:
- **`apps/web`** — Next.js 16 App Router frontend (TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui, TanStack Query)
- **`apps/api`** — Express.js + Prisma backend (TypeScript, Zod, JWT, Passport.js, Winston)
- **`packages/*`** — Shared configs, UI components (`@repo/ui`), validators (`@repo/validators`), types (`@repo/types`)

---

## 0. Universal Rules (all files in the monorepo)

- Never use `any` — use `unknown`, generics, or explicit interfaces.
- Never commit `.env` with real values; only `.env.example` is committed.
- Remove unused imports and `console.log` before committing.
- Follow Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`.
- ESLint and Prettier are always enforced — no inline disables without a comment explaining why.
- Prettier: `singleQuote: false`, `trailingComma: "none"`, `printWidth: 100`.
- All secrets must come from environment variables; never hardcode credentials.
- Magic strings/numbers must be extracted into named constants.
- Functions must have a single responsibility and stay under ~60 lines.

---

## 1. Monorepo & Turborepo

- All shared code lives in `packages/` — never duplicate it inside `apps/`.
- Internal packages use `@repo/*` namespace.
- Types shared across apps → `packages/types`.
- Zod schemas shared across apps → `packages/validators`.
- Build pipeline is defined in `turbo.json`; declare all tasks there for proper caching.
- Run everything from root: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`.

---

## 2. TypeScript

- Strict mode is on everywhere.
- `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections/mapped types.
- Frontend type names: `PascalCase`, no `I` prefix (e.g., `User`, `LoginData`).
- Backend type names: `PascalCase`, `I` prefix for interfaces (e.g., `IUser`, `ILoginData`) — existing convention.
- Type files: `kebab-case` naming (e.g., `auth.ts`, `user.ts`).
- Enums: `PascalCase` name, `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` values.

---

## 3. Naming Conventions

| Entity | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files & folders | `kebab-case` | `auth-service.ts`, `user-list/` |
| React components | `PascalCase` | `UserList.tsx` |
| shadcn/ui files | `kebab-case` | `button.tsx` |
| Hook files | `kebab-case`, `use-` prefix | `use-auth.ts` |
| Hook functions | `camelCase`, `use` prefix | `useAuth()` |
| API Services | `PascalCase` singleton | `AuthService` |
| API Controllers | `PascalCase` singleton | `AuthController` |
| Constants | `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | `MAX_FILE_SIZE` |
| Zod schemas | `camelCase` + `ZodSchema` | `createUserZodSchema` |

---

## 4. Security

- Validate ALL user input with Zod before processing — no raw `req.body` in services.
- Hash passwords with `bcrypt` (≥10 rounds) — never store plaintext.
- JWT secrets from environment variables only — never hardcoded.
- Auth routes protected by `auth` middleware; role routes also by `authorizeRoles`.
- CORS: explicit allowlist — no wildcard `*` in production.
- Cookies: `httpOnly`, `secure`, `sameSite` always set.
- Never log passwords, tokens, or PII.
- Never expose stack traces or internal errors in production API responses.

---

## 5. Error Handling

### Backend
- Services throw `ApiError(statusCode, message)` for domain errors — never plain `Error`.
- All controller handlers wrapped in `catchAsync`.
- `globalErrorHandler` handles ZodError, PrismaClientValidationError, TokenExpiredError, ApiError, Error.

### Frontend
- Data-fetching errors must surface as toast notifications — never silently swallowed.
- Every `useQuery`/`useMutation` must handle loading and error states visually.

---

## 6. Frontend Rules — `apps/web`

### Structure
```
src/
  app/           # Pages, layouts, route handlers (App Router)
  components/
    layouts/     # Header, Footer — PascalCase
    ui/          # shadcn/ui — kebab-case, DO NOT modify
    widgets/     # Feature composites — kebab-case folders, PascalCase files
    icons/       # PascalCase + Icon suffix (e.g., ReactIcon)
  config/        # seo.ts, site.ts
  data/          # Static data — kebab-case, variableName ends with Data
  helpers/       # Domain computation helpers
  hooks/         # use-*.ts custom hooks
  lib/           # api.ts, date.ts, cookie-client.ts
  providers/     # React Context providers — PascalCase
  styles/        # tailwind.css
  types/         # Type definitions — kebab-case files
```

### Components
- Every component folder must have `index.ts` re-exporting it.
- `components/ui` (shadcn/ui) is off-limits — wrap instead of modifying.
- No inline styles — Tailwind only.
- Prop names must be intent-driven: `onSubmit`, `isLoading`, `variant`.

### Data Fetching
- HTTP requests via helpers in `src/lib/api.ts` (Axios-based).
- TanStack Query (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) for all server state.
- Always show loading/error states.
- Errors → toast notifications.

### State
- React Context for global UI state in `src/providers/`.
- Avoid `useState` for server state — use TanStack Query.

### Environment
- `@t3-oss/env-nextjs` + Zod validation in `src/env.ts`.
- Import env values only from `src/env.ts`.
- Client vars must have `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix.

### Routing & Cookies
- App Router conventions: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- Server cookies: `cookies()` from `next/headers`.
- Client cookies: helpers from `src/lib/cookie-client.ts`.

### Themes & Fonts
- Theme CSS variables managed by `ThemePresetProvider` via injected `<style>` tag.
- Font CSS variables (`--font-sans`, `--font-serif`, `--font-mono`) are set per theme.
- Google Fonts loaded as `<link>` tags in `layout.tsx` head — not via CSS `@import`.

### Accessibility
- Every interactive element has an accessible label.
- Use ARIA attributes where semantic HTML is insufficient.
- Meaningful images wrapped in `<figure>` with `<figcaption>`.

### Icons
- `lucide-react` only. No mixing of icon libraries.

### Utilities
- Date → `src/lib/date.ts`
- Numbers/currency → `Intl` API
- Slugs → `@sindresorhus/slugify`
- General hooks → `usehooks-ts`
- Constants → `src/constants/` in `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`

---

## 7. Backend Rules — `apps/api`

### Structure
```
src/
  app/
    middlewares/   # auth.ts, globalErrorHandler.ts, validateRequest.ts
    modules/       # Feature modules
      <module>/
        <module>.controller.ts
        <module>.service.ts
        <module>.route.ts
        <module>.validation.ts
  config/          # index.ts, passport.ts, strategies/
  DB/              # Prisma client init
  enums/           # Shared enums
  errors/          # ApiError.ts, handleZodError.ts, handleValidationError.ts
  helpers/         # emailHelper.ts, jwtHelper.ts
  routes/          # Root router index.ts
  shared/          # catchAsync.ts, sendResponse.ts, logger.ts, prisma.ts
  types/           # IUser, ILoginData, etc.
  util/            # generateOTP.ts, cryptoToken.ts
  app.ts           # Express app (middlewares, CORS, session, routes)
  server.ts        # HTTP server entry point
```

### Module Pattern
Each feature module contains exactly 4 files:
1. **`<module>.validation.ts`** — Zod schemas (`create<Action>ZodSchema`)
2. **`<module>.route.ts`** — Router: mount `validateRequest` → controller
3. **`<module>.controller.ts`** — `catchAsync` + call service + `sendResponse`
4. **`<module>.service.ts`** — Business logic + Prisma queries + `ApiError` throws

### Response Format
```ts
// Success (via sendResponse)
{ success: true, statusCode: 200, message: "...", data: {...} | null }

// Error (via globalErrorHandler)
{ success: false, message: "...", errorMessages: [{path, message}], stack?: "..." }
```

### Database & Prisma
- Shared Prisma client from `src/shared/prisma.ts` only.
- Use `findUnique` for unique field lookups.
- Select only needed fields — no implicit `SELECT *`.
- Multi-step operations → `prisma.$transaction([...])`.
- Schema changes → `prisma migrate dev` only.

### Auth & Authorization
- JWT: short-lived access token + long-lived refresh token.
- `auth` middleware verifies JWT and attaches `req.user`.
- `authorizeRoles(...roles)` for role-based protection on top of `auth`.
- OAuth via Passport.js strategies in `src/config/strategies/`.
- Sessions for OAuth: `httpOnly`, `secure`, `sameSite` cookie flags.

### Logging
- Winston (`src/shared/logger.ts`) for structured logs.
- Morgan for HTTP request logging (separate success/error streams).
- Never log sensitive data.
- Development: `info`; Production: `warn`/`error` only.

### Config
- All env values loaded in `src/config/index.ts`.
- Never access `process.env` directly in business logic — always via `config`.
- Keep `.env.example` in sync with every new variable.

---

## 8. Precedence

- Repository rules in this file take precedence over any global Cursor defaults.
- `apps/web` and `apps/api` specific conventions take precedence over the shared rules above when they conflict.
